    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/1/71078.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 6,
    "turn_text": "Well, I get correct. And, you know, you think back into my dad's day, IT was not, you know, it wasn't a feature of healthcare now. It's something with which people have to live. And sometimes it's helpful. Sometimes it's the opposite of helpful. but it is part of the world. And certainly, I think as people who take care of patients, we, in order to do the best job possible, we need to be facile and we need to be flexible enough to allow that to be a useful part of our patient's experience.",
